1. Correct application of Ending with a Preposition (Myths); before/after shows intentional change; explanation names the grammar job.
2. Correct application of Ending with a Preposition (Myths); before/after shows intentional change; explanation names the grammar job.
3. Correct application of Ending with a Preposition (Myths); before/after shows intentional change; explanation names the grammar job.
4. Correct application of Ending with a Preposition (Myths); before/after shows intentional change; explanation names the grammar job.
5. Correct application of Ending with a Preposition (Myths); before/after shows intentional change; explanation names the grammar job.
6. Correct application of Ending with a Preposition (Myths); before/after shows intentional change; explanation names the grammar job.

</details>

## Exit ticket

1. In one sentence, what does “Ending with a Preposition (Myths)” help a reader or writer do?
2. Name the common mistake to avoid today (hint: related to treating two true facts as if…).
3. Create one new practice item (with answer) a classmate could try in 2 minutes.

